\ ==== lib units ====

\ Standard units provided by lib.telic (SI + currencies), used directly — no
\ redeclaration. Guards the built-in unit set against regression.
10 m . cr
3 kg 2 m * 1 s / 1 s / . cr
100 watt 5 ampere / . cr
1 km 500 m + . cr
2 hour 30 minute + . cr
5 $ 2 $ + . cr
1 $ 50 ¢ + . cr
3 £ . cr
2 € . cr
[ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 2 matrix km  [ 1000 2000 3000 4000 ] 2 2 matrix m  + . cr
1 $ 1 £ +

clear

\ ==== constants ====

\ mathematical constants: computed, not typed
PI . E . TAU . PHI . cr
PI 2 * TAU = . cr
PHI 1 - 1 PHI / = . cr

\ physical constants are dimensioned quantities
C . cr
G . cr
H . cr
HBAR . cr
KB . NA . QE . cr

\ unit algebra composes them
KB 300 kelvin * . cr
C 2 ^ 1 kg * . cr
H TAU / HBAR = . cr

\ constants cannot be reassigned
9 to PI

clear

\ ==== units ====

\ Comprehensive dimensioned-quantity test: declaration, arithmetic with unit
\ propagation, dimensionless collapse, scaled units, cross-scale add/compare,
\ power/sqrt/negate/abs, dimensioned matrices, error paths, and an image
\ round-trip. Batch mode: every line's exact stdout is the golden output.

\ ---- base dimensions ----
base unit m
base unit s
base unit kg

\ ---- application (dounit), top-level and compiled ----
10 m . cr
3 kg . cr
: dist 10 m ;
dist . cr

\ ---- multiplication: compound and scalar ----
3 m 4 m * . cr
10 m 2 * . cr
2 10 m * . cr

\ ---- division: compound and dimensionless collapse ----
10 m 2 s / . cr
10 m 2 m / . cr

\ ---- derived unit built by arithmetic, named, then interning reuses name ----
1 kg 1 m * 1 s / 1 s / unit newton
3 newton . cr
2 kg 3 m * 1 s / 1 s / . cr

\ ---- addition / subtraction, same unit ----
3 m 4 m + . cr
10 m 3 m - . cr

\ ---- power / sqrt on quantities ----
3 m 2 ^ . cr
2 m 3 ^ . cr
9 m 9 m * sqrt . cr
9 m 9 m * 0.5 ^ . cr

\ ---- negate / abs keep the unit ----
3 m negate . cr
3 m negate abs . cr

\ ---- comparison, same unit ----
3 m 2 m < . cr
2 m 3 m < . cr
3 m 3 m = . cr

\ ---- scaled units: declare the smaller as base ----
base unit cent
100 cent unit dollar
3 dollar . cr
5 cent . cr

\ ---- cross-scale add: result in the left operand's unit ----
1 dollar 50 cent + . cr
50 cent 1 dollar + . cr

\ ---- cross-scale comparison: value-normalized ----
100 cent 1 dollar = . cr
50 cent 1 dollar < . cr
1 dollar 50 cent < . cr

\ ---- unnamed compound inheriting a scale folds to base names ----
base unit ml
1000 ml unit l
2 l 4 s / . cr

\ ---- error paths ----
3 m 4 s +
3 m 2 +
3 m 2 m ^
3 m 0.01 ^
3 m 1e30 ^                              \ (exponent overflows a 32-bit rational)
3 m -1e30 ^                             \ (negative exponent overflows too)
3 m sin
base unit foo
1 foo 2 sqrt / unit irrational

\ ---- dimensioned matrices ----
[ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 2 matrix m . cr
[ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 2 matrix m  [ 1 1 1 1 ] 2 2 matrix m  + . cr
[ 4 6 8 10 ] 2 2 matrix m  2 m /  . cr

\ ---- named and compound units render ----
10 m . cr
5 newton . cr
1 dollar 50 cent + . cr

\ ---- cancellation folds the scale ratio into the magnitude ----
60 s unit minute
1 minute 1 s / . cr                     \ 60
100 cent 1 dollar / . cr                \ 1
1 dollar 100 cent / . cr                \ 1
2 dollar 40 cent / . cr                 \ 5
3 m 3 m / . cr                          \ 1
1 minute 1 minute *  1 s 1 s *  / . cr  \ 3600

\ ---- scale product that exceeds int range errors instead of wrapping ----
100000 m unit bigm
1 bigm 1 bigm *

clear
\ ---- unit-of: a quantity's unit as the quantity 1 in that unit ----
10 m unit-of . cr                       \ 1 m
[ 10 20 ] vector m unit-of . cr         \ 1 m   (matrix magnitude, scalar unit back)
10 m 2 s / unit-of . cr                 \ 1 m.s^-1 (computed unit)
5 unit-of . cr                          \ 1     (bare value, dimensionless)
0 m unit-of . cr                        \ 1 m   (zero magnitude is fine)
[ ] vector s unit-of 1 s = . cr         \ 1     (empty typed column keeps its unit)
10 m unit-of 1 s = . cr                 \ 0
7 m 7 m unit-of * . cr                  \ 7 m^2 (attach a unit by multiplying)

clear
\ ---- a new name for an already-named unit is a synonym, not a rename: the
\ existing unit keeps its name and the alias renders under it ----
1 m unit meter
5 m . cr                                \ 5 m      (m is not renamed)
5 meter . cr                            \ 5 m      (the alias resolves to m)
5 meter 3 m + . cr                      \ 8 m      (interconvertible)
1 1 s / unit hz2
5 hertz . cr                            \ 5 hertz  (hertz is not renamed)

clear
\ ---- IEC binary data units, powers of 1024 (MiB is the base dimension) ----
1 KiB 1 B / . cr                        \ 1024
1 MiB 1 KiB / . cr                      \ 1024
1 GiB 1 MiB / . cr                      \ 1024
1 TiB 1 GiB / . cr                      \ 1024
1 PiB 1 TiB / . cr                      \ 1024
4 GiB 1 B / . cr                        \ 4294967296  (4 * 2^30)
1536 MiB 1 GiB + 1 GiB / . cr           \ 2.5   (mixed-unit arithmetic reconciles)
512 MiB . cr                            \ 512 MiB
1 PiB . cr                              \ 1 PiB

clear
\ ---- as: re-express a quantity in the unit an xt attaches (' MiB) ----
2 34 ^ B ' MiB as . cr                  \ 16384 MiB
2 34 ^ B ' GiB as . cr                  \ 16 GiB
2 34 ^ B ' MiB as magnitude . cr        \ 16384   (bare count)
1 $ ' ¢ as . cr                         \ 100 ¢   (general, not memory-only)
5 ' MiB as                              \ (cannot convert a bare number)

clear
